<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="0cdaea92-e31c-5dce-9b38-6632ead5a755" activityNameId="70c7359e-2db6-538a-90b0-fbeedf5ea722" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">HDD, laptop computer, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: HDD, laptop computer, at plant
After 2023 updates, this dataset can be applied to describe the production of a common hard disk drive in the reference year 2019 (2.5 inch or 63.5 mm of radius, up to 1 TB, total weight 0.09 kg). New composition is gathered from JRC technical reports and manufacturer's product sheet. The dataset includes material information for all the major hard disk drive components (covers, printed wiring board, circular plates (platters), pointer assembly, etc.). The information is mainly based on one dissertation work plus laptop-specific data provided by a leading HDD manufacturer. Data for the desktop HDD have been extrapolated to the lighter laptop HDD by specific calculation setups.; UUID: 2b9f4897-94f6-365b-be05-fc01a7651919
Describes the production of a hard disk drive for a laptop computer. Calculated per 1 produced hard disk (1 unit). Included are the materials (mainly metals and plastics) with their respective manufacturing processes (e.g. sheet rolling or blow moulding). Further inventoried is the infrastructure (factory), the electricity for the assembly of the hard disk drive, the respective waste heat, and the required rail and road transport for input materials from the regional storage to the factory. Not included are emissions to air and water (negligible), the heating of the facility, scrap materials (recycled and reused), the packaging, as well as the disposal, which is attributed to the desktop computer as a whole.
Location: A laptop hard disk drive may be assembled anywhere in the world.
Technology: The production of a hard disk drive for a laptop computer includes the metal processing steps rolling, cutting, section bar extrusion and coating. Plastic parts are blow moulded or extruded into required shapes.
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: unknown
Sampling: Own estimations based on literature. Weighing of original components happened at a Technical University after professional disassembly.
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2b9f4897-94f6-365b-be05-fc01a7651919.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
